cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite CalmSense when using this software."
type: software
title: "CalmSense: Subject-Independent Stress Detection and Calibration on WESAD"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-03
url: "https://github.com/urmeo/CalmSense"
repository-code: "https://github.com/urmeo/CalmSense"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Bose"
    given-names: "Urme"
keywords:
  - stress-detection
  - wearables
  - physiological-signals
  - heart-rate-variability
  - electrodermal-activity
  - leave-one-subject-out
  - model-calibration
  - reproducible-research
  - wesad
abstract: >-
  CalmSense evaluates wearable stress detection on WESAD using Leave-One-Subject-Out
  testing. It includes signal processing, 60 registered features (58 in the saved
  benchmark), classical classifiers, a 1D-CNN, SHAP, calibration, decision curves,
  personalization, and cross-dataset transfer.
